{
  "verdict": "changes_required",
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "P1",
      "file": "supabase/migrations/20260907180100_background_generation_schedule.sql",
      "issue": "The cron dispatcher posts to /functions/v1/generation-jobs with only Content-Type and x-pragma-worker-token — no Authorization/apikey. Unless the function is deployed with verify_jwt disabled, the gateway rejects the call with 401 before any handler code runs, and no config entry for this is included in the change. Server-side recovery after all tabs close would then silently never happen: jobs stay 'running' with a 'waiting' provider step and results are effectively lost (paid-for responses never harvested), with no alert because dispatch_generation_jobs ignores the net.http_post outcome.",
      "fix": "Add the deployment config for this function (e.g. supabase/config.toml [functions.generation-jobs] verify_jwt = false) in this change, and/or include the service-role Authorization + apikey headers in the net.http_post call. Add a check that the dispatch actually reaches the worker (e.g. log net response ids / a last_dispatch_at column) so a broken schedule is observable."
    },
    {
      "severity": "P1",
      "file": "supabase/functions/generation-jobs/index.ts",
      "issue": "Start is deduplicated by UNIQUE(owner_id, request_key) with upsert ignoreDuplicates:true, and request_key does not include job outcome. Once a job for a request reaches status 'failed' (including failures that never touched the provider: missing OPENAI_API_KEY, release_id mismatch, 'save 실패/권한 만료', 2h age guard, or an internal invoke error), any subsequent 'start' with the same body/scenario revision returns that same failed row, and invokeAstraMission immediately rethrows job.error. There is no reset/requeue/delete path (only SELECT/INSERT/UPDATE granted, no admin-facing retry action), so a transient failure permanently blocks regeneration of that mission until the scenario's updated_at changes or the release id changes.",
      "fix": "Distinguish safe-to-retry failures from ambiguous ones: on 'start', if the existing row is 'failed' and contains no step in state 'submitting'/'waiting' (i.e. no possible outstanding provider charge), requeue it (status='queued', error=NULL, steps='[]', next_run_at=now(), new lease cleared) instead of returning the stale error; otherwise return the response ids for manual reconciliation. Expose an explicit admin 'retry' action for that transition."
    },
    {
      "severity": "P1",
      "file": "supabase/functions/generation-jobs/index.ts",
      "issue": "tick() calls handleGenerateScenario with an internally constructed Request that carries no Authorization/apikey header. If the existing generate-scenario handler performs its own admin/JWT check (as the browser-facing endpoint), every job fails on the first tick with an auth error, which is then latched as status='failed' and — per the dedup issue above — permanently blocks that request. Additionally, importing ../generate-scenario/index.ts pulls in that module's top-level side effects (its own Deno.serve registration) into this function's isolate.",
      "fix": "Verify and, if needed, extract handleGenerateScenario into a side-effect-free shared module (no top-level Deno.serve) and have it accept an already-authorized caller context, or forward a service-role/internal-trust marker on the internal Request so the internal invocation is not rejected. Add one integration test that runs tick() end-to-end against a stubbed provider to prove the internal invocation is authorized."
    },
    {
      "severity": "P2",
      "file": "supabase/migrations/20260907180100_background_generation_schedule.sql",
      "issue": "pg_net is created WITH SCHEMA extensions while the dispatcher calls net.http_post. If the installed pg_net places its functions in the schema given at CREATE EXTENSION time (or rejects the relocation), the migration or the dispatcher call fails at runtime, disabling recovery.",
      "fix": "Match the schema actually used by the deployed pg_net (create without WITH SCHEMA, or fully qualify the call to the schema where http_post exists) and assert it in a migration-time smoke check."
    },
    {
      "severity": "P2",
      "file": "supabase/functions/generation-jobs/index.ts",
      "issue": "Recovery throughput: the cron fires once per minute and each worker invocation claims exactly one job and advances exactly one provider step, while next_run_at is set to now()+5s. With tabs closed, a multi-step job advances one step per minute and N pending jobs are serialized, so long queues drift far behind the 2h age guard that hard-fails jobs.",
      "fix": "Loop tick() inside the worker invocation until no job is claimable or a time budget is reached, and/or dispatch several parallel worker requests per cron run; align the 2h guard with realistic worst-case recovery throughput."
    },
    {
      "severity": "P2",
      "file": "supabase/functions/_shared/backgroundGeneration.ts",
      "issue": "The `if (index >= 16)` cap is evaluated before cached steps are replayed, so a job that legitimately recorded more than 16 steps can never be replayed to completion (its stored results become unreachable). Also GenerationStopped(step.error) can be constructed with undefined, yielding an unhelpful 'undefined' error surfaced to admins.",
      "fix": "Apply the call-limit check only when a new step would be created (i.e. when args.steps[index] is absent), and default step.error to a explanatory message when rethrowing a stored stop."
    }
  ]
}
